  "2026-11-05T10:52:21.298Z",codex-agent,"Seeded model passed 500 random sequences against SDK read-back. Packed npm and Bun journeys passed with Git absent, including npx bunx native SDK TOON JSON and refused writes. Public scratch tracker-copy measurement read 173 items, defined 38 distinct terms and 44 senses, resolved 42 of 42 scoped probes and abstained on all 10 ambiguous or unknown probes. Three bounded packets retained witnesses: 35580 bytes and 8896 estimated tokens versus 130362 bytes and 32591 tokens of selected source passages, saving 72.71 percent; wall time 17104 ms. Bindings are explicitly deferred by the first-slice plan."
  "2026-11-05T11:26:54.364Z",codex-agent,"Final review tightened JSON submissions to reject inherited, accessor and hidden properties before reading them, and checked same-line independent statement counters with a positive tooling fixture. All 40 tests passed in the previous full run; one valid-contrast branch was missing and now has a regression assertion. The stricter gate correctly refused that 99.55 percent branch result rather than rounding it to approval. A redundant Windows privacy pattern triggered the identity scanner; the shared separator pattern covers that case and its refusal corpus now includes a Windows-shaped example."
  "2026-11-05T12:34:04.377Z",codex-agent,"Budget-hint boundary experiment found 10 of 20 SDK minimum estimates did not fit when retried exactly, because receipt digits changed. The package now verifies retry budgets in at most four fitter passes and reports no usable budget above the hard ceiling. Twenty exact-retry probes and failing-fitter cases pass. The real-data proof now directly pins four copied tracker descriptions as a fourth scope; reviewed meanings distinguish release verification from package publication. Current receipt: 38 terms, 48 senses, 46/46 scoped probes, 10/10 abstentions, 40217 packet bytes and 10056 estimated tokens versus 132732 source-passage bytes and 33183 tokens, saving 69.70 percent in 18880 ms. Every expected and actual probe and the refused budget are recorded in docs/real-data.md."
  "2026-11-05T12:50:06.361Z",codex-agent,"Final npm run release:check passed all 13 stages under an isolated HOME with Git global and system config disabled: 40 tests passed, zero failures or skips; independent emitted-source coverage 426/426 statements, 271/271 branches, 108/108 functions and 360/360 lines across nine runtime modules. Packed acceptance passed two Git-free npm and native Bun journeys using one unchanged archive and npx/bunx host dispatch. Behavioral revert gate produced all three expected failures; unchanged implementation then passed both selected regressions. Bun gate is running serially. Exact native cost/cursor compatibility remains the separate yrza release blocker."
  "2026-11-05T13:05:07.020Z",codex-agent,"The corrected domain head passed the previous 13-stage npm gate: 41 tests, 428/428 statements, 275/275 branches, 108/108 functions and 362/362 lines. Additional CI reproduction found pm health --strict-exit also mandates optional Git integration, even in a clean standalone clone. Public RunHealthOptions documents that coupling. CI now uses scripts/tracker-health.ts and fails on the authoritative SDK result.ok with checkOnly/full enabled and requireMergeDrivers false; durable integrity, history drift and extension checks remain enforced. A real plain tracker passes and deliberately corrupted scratch history exits nonzero. No merge installation, configuration or history repair was performed. The new tracker:health stage brings release:check to 14 stages. Both full gates will certify this final tooling change."
